omx-panel (0.17.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ci, release: a job reading the wave's devel channel reads its base wave
    too
  * layout: a matrix row empty at every drawn head takes no row (drawnLines),
    in the face and the renderer alike
  * group model L6: a row the drawn heads leave empty takes no row, as a head
    beyond the count takes no column
  * renderer: a panel of seven sections or more is as tall as its sections
  * renderer tests: the host side is omx-panel picture's defaultState, not a
    copy of it
  * omx-panel picture: a plugin's panel drawn from its declaration alone into
    a PNG
  * runtime install: a recommendation takes this build's packages, never
    downgrading omx-panel
  * base: a built-from-unknown refusal carries git's own word
  * ci: build and lint the DEB may read its checkout with git, so the base
    knows its commit
  * ci: the package and offline builds run in the job's own container,
    reading the channel add-openmixer adds
  * ci: the jobs that run the tree read omx-dsp and omx-contract from the
    channel, linked as the packages' builds link them
  * renderer: omx_panel_ui.h is a documented header, and the declarations
    added since the baseline are documented
  * meter-surfaces: the bar and the marker are read inside the meter's frame,
    where they are drawn
  * store: the plugin-db domain is read from the contract directory
    libomx-domain names, and none found is refused by name
  * ci: no Debian bookworm cell (owner 2026-11-27: bookworm is dropped from
    the matrix)
  * changelog: 0.17.3 names the prebuilt base, CLAP in omx-panel sync and its
    triggers (#284)
  * ci: a wave's run admits its devel channel and staging in the
    from-the-channel guard
  * ci: a dispatch off main in a wave reads that wave's devel channel too, as
    it reads staging
  * ci: a pull request into devel in a wave reads that wave's devel channel
    above staging
  * release: omx-panel 0.17.3 (0.17.2 to 0.17.3), a patch
  * describe: a served display's kind is the scan's number, read as its panel
    word
  * base: the omx-plugins set's inputs, from the channel's omx-plugins 0.21.0
    (#284)
  * omx-panel sync lists CLAP plugins, the pass runs on its own triggers, and
    the base is held to its reference sets (#284)
  * docs/descriptions-store.md: the base holds omx-plugins in both formats,
    the pass lists CLAP plugins and has triggers of its own (#284)
  * tools/vocabulary.mjs: pkg-config is asked each variable once per process
    (#282)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:27:29 +0000
